# Testing and performance

For any poker math/domain change:
- add/update unit tests;
- include edge cases;
- include at least one regression test for each fixed bug.

Required categories as applicable:
- golden scenario tests;
- invariants;
- blockers/card uniqueness;
- betting legality;
- split pots/ties;
- seeded equity tests.

Never change expected values only to make tests pass without explaining why the old expectation was wrong.

Heavy equity calculations must not block the browser main thread.
Worker responses must not race: stale requests cannot overwrite a newer calculation.

Performance changes should report measured before/after values when a benchmark already exists.
Correctness has priority over micro-optimization.
